":"RWDD3","gene_id":"ENSG00000122481","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.816994,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.021913,"nucleus_score":-0.36407,"pct_ad":0.256338,"pct_control":0.258086,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":-0.0786924,"donor_lfcse":0.0903759,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-1.00469e-05},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"RWDD3","gene_symbol_current":"RWDD3","gene_id":"ENSG00000122481","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.130949,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0362275,"nucleus_score":-1.6262,"pct_ad":0.150235,"pct_control":0.154912,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.886226,"donor_log2fc":-0.0833231,"donor_lfcse":0.103093,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00807193}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000122481","module":"turquoise","kme":0.112336,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.796936,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000122481","entrez_id":["25950"],"uniprot":["Q9Y3V2"],"ncbi_summary":"Involved in negative regulation of NF-kappaB transcription factor activity; positive regulation of hypoxia-inducible factor-1alpha signaling pathway; and positive regulation of protein sumoylation. Predicted to be located in cytoplasm and nucleus. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9Y3V2","text":"Enhancer of SUMO conjugation. Via its interaction with UBE2I/UBC9, increases SUMO conjugation to proteins by promoting the binding of E1 and E2 enzymes, thioester linkage between SUMO and UBE2I/UBC9 and transfer of SUMO to specific target proteins which include HIF1A, PIAS, NFKBIA, NR3C1 and TOP1. Isoform 1 and isoform 2 positively regulate the NF-kappa-B signaling pathway by enhancing the sumoylation of NF-kappa-B inhibitor alpha (NFKBIA), promoting its stabilization which consequently leads to an increased inhibition of NF-kappa-B transcriptional activity. Isoform 1 and isoform 2 negatively regulate the hypoxia-inducible factor-1 alpha (HIF1A) signaling pathway by increasing the sumoylation of HIF1A, promoting its stabilization, transcriptional activity and the expression of its target gene VEGFA during hypoxia. Isoform 2 promotes the sumoylation and transcriptional activity of the glucocorticoid receptor NR3C1 and enhances the interaction of SUMO1 and NR3C1 with UBE2I/UBC9. Has no effect on ubiquitination."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}